```java
import android.net.HttpURLConnection;
import android.net.URL;

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {
        // Create a URL object
        URL url = new URL("http://example.com/compressed-url");

        // Open a connection to the URL
        HttpURLConnection connection = (HttpURLConnection) url.openConnection();

        // Set the request method to GET
        connection.setRequestMethod("GET");

        // Get the response code
        int responseCode = (int) connection.getResponseCode();

        // Get the location header
        String location = connection.getHeaderField("Location");

        // Print the full URL
        System.out.println(location);
    }
}
```

In this code, we first create a `URL` object and open a connection to it. We then set the request method to GET and get the response code. Finally, we get the `Location` header using the `getHeaderField()` method and print the full URL.

