Here's a sample Java code snippet that opens a JOptionPane with the error message and formatted stack trace of the throwable in a scrollable text area:

```java
import javax.swing.*;
import java.io.PrintWriter;
import java.io.StringWriter;
import java.lang.Thread.UncaughtExceptionHandler;

public class ErrorDialog {
    public static void showErrorMessage(Throwable throwable) {
        String errorMessage = throwable.toString();
        String stackTrace = getStackTrace(throwable);

        // Create a new JFrame to hold the text area
        JFrame frame = new JFrame("Error Message");
        frame.setDefaultCloseOperation(JFrame.DISPOSE_ON_CLOSE);
        frame.setSize(400, 300);

        // Create a new JTextArea to display the error message and stack trace
        JTextArea textArea = new JTextArea(10, 30);
        textArea.setEditable(false);
        textArea.setText(errorMessage + "\n" + stackTrace);

        // Create a new JScrollPane to hold the text area
        JScrollPane scrollPane = new JScrollPane(textArea);

        // Add the scroll pane to the frame
        frame.getContentPane().add(scrollPane, BorderLayout.CENTER);

        // Display the dialog
        JOptionPane.showMessageDialog(frame, "Error", "Error Message", JOptionPane.ERROR_MESSAGE);
    }

    private static String getStackTrace(Throwable throwable) {
        StringWriter stringWriter = new StringWriter();
        PrintWriter printWriter = new PrintWriter(stringWriter);
        throwable.printStackTrace(printWriter);
        return stringWriter.toString();
    }
}
```

This code snippet defines a method `showErrorMessage` that takes a `Throwable` object as input and displays an error message dialog with the error message and formatted stack trace in a scrollable text area. The `getStackTrace` method is used to extract the stack trace from the `Throwable` object.

