Here is a simple implementation of a LinkedList from varargs in Java:

```java
import java.util.*;

public class VarargsLinkedList {
    private Node head;
    private Node tail;
    private int size;

    private class Node {
        int data;
        Node next;

        public Node(int data) {
            this.data = data;
            this.next = null;
        }
    }

    public VarargsLinkedList() {
        head = null;
        tail = null;
        size = 0;
    }

    public void add(int... args) {
        for (int arg : args) {
            Node newNode = new Node(arg);
            if (head == null) {
                head = newNode;
                tail = newNode;
            } else {
                tail.next = newNode;
                tail = newNode;
            }
            size++;
        }
    }

    public void printList() {
        Node temp = head;
        while (temp != null) {
            System.out.print(temp.data + " ");
            temp = temp.next;
        }
        System.out.println();
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        VarargsLinkedList list = new VarargsLinkedList();
        list.add(1, 2, 3, 4, 5);
        list.printList(); // prints: 1 2 3 4 5
    }
}
```

This implementation uses a Node class to represent each element in the linked list, and a VarargsLinkedList class to manage the list. The add method adds elements to the end of the list, and the printList method prints the elements in the list.

