2. `java.util.Date`: This class represents a specific point in time and time zone. It serves as a way to represent a date and time in a more human-readable format, but it can be converted to seconds using the `getTime()` method.

3. `java.time.Instant`: This class represents an instant in time, including the year, month, day, hour, minute, second, and nanosecond. It serves as a more precise way to represent a point in time, and it can be converted to seconds using the `toEpochSecond()` method.

