### Java API Methods for Obtaining Bean Info

#### 1. `java.beans.Introspector.getBeanInfo()`

This method serves to introspect a Java Bean and retrieve information about its properties, exposed methods, and events. It also checks if the BeanInfo class has been previously introspected and returns it from the cache if so.

#### 2. `java.lang.Object.getClass()`

This method returns the runtime class of the given object, which is the class that the object is an instance of. It serves as a way to obtain the class of an object at runtime.

### Example Usage

Here's an example of how to use these methods to obtain the BeanInfo for a bean class:

```java
import java.beans.BeanInfo;
import java.beans.Introspector;
import java.lang.reflect.Method;

// Assume we have a bean class called "MyBean"
class MyBean {
    private String name;
    private int age;

    public MyBean(String name, int age) {
        this.name = name;
        this.age = age;
    }

    public String getName() {
        return name;
    }

    public void setName(String name) {
        this.name = name;
    }

    public int getAge() {
        return age;
    }

    public void setAge(int age) {
        this.age = age;
    }
}

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        // Get the BeanInfo for MyBean
        BeanInfo beanInfo = Introspector.getBeanInfo(MyBean.class);

        // Get the properties of MyBean
        Method[] methods = beanInfo.getAttributes();
        for (Method method : methods) {
            System.out.println(method.getName());
        }

        // Get the methods of MyBean
        Method[] methods2 = beanInfo.getEventMethods();
        for (Method method : methods2) {
            System.out.println(method.getName());
        }
    }
}
```

In this example, we use `Introspector.getBeanInfo()` to get the BeanInfo for the `MyBean` class, and then use the `getAttributes()` and `getEventMethods()` methods to retrieve the properties and methods of the bean.

