This method serves to replace all occurrences of a specified pattern in a string with a replacement string. It takes a `Matcher` object and a replacement string as arguments, and returns the modified string.

### 5. `java.util.regex.Matcher.quoteReplacement()`

This method serves to quote a replacement string so that it is treated as a literal string, rather than a regular expression pattern. It takes a replacement string as an argument, and returns the quoted replacement string.

