- `java.net.InetAddress.getLoopbackAddress()`: This method returns the IP address of the loopback interface, which is the interface that is always available and never goes down. It serves as a default value for the `getByInetAddress` method.

- `java.net.NetworkInterface.getByInetAddress(InetAddress)`: This method returns the network interface that corresponds to the specified IP address. It serves as a way to get the network interface that corresponds to a specific IP address.

- `java.net.NetworkInterface.getHardwareAddress()`: This method returns the hardware address (usually MAC) of the interface if it has one and if it can be accessed given the current privileges. It serves as a way to get the MAC address of the network interface.

- `java.net.UnknownHostException`: This exception is thrown when the specified IP address is not recognized. It serves as a way to handle the case where the IP address is not valid.

