3. `java.lang.reflect.Method.getAnnotation()`: This method retrieves the annotation associated with the specified method. It serves as the mechanism for checking if a method is annotated with the specified annotation.

4. `java.lang.reflect.Method.invoke()`: This method invokes the specified method on the target instance. It serves as the mechanism for delegating method invocations to the target instance when the method is not annotated with the specified annotation.

5. `java.lang.reflect.Proxy.getProxyClass()`: This method returns the proxy class for the specified interfaces. It serves as a helper method for `Proxy.newProxyInstance()` to determine the proxy class.

