To achieve the requested functionality, you can use a combination of these methods. Here's an example of how you can create a wrapped runnable that ensures that if an exception occurs during the execution, the specified exception handler is invoked:

```java
public class WrappedRunnable implements Runnable {
    private final Runnable target;
    private final Thread.UncaughtExceptionHandler exceptionHandler;

    public WrappedRunnable(Runnable target, Thread.UncaughtExceptionHandler exceptionHandler) {
        this.target = target;
        this.exceptionHandler = exceptionHandler;
    }

