   - If `true`, the border is painted, effectively making the button visible, and if `false`, the border is not painted, making the button appear invisible.

2. `setBorder(Border border)`: 
   - This method serves to set the border of the button. 
   - By setting the border to an empty border (e.g., `BorderFactory.createEmptyBorder(0, 0, 0, 0)`), you can effectively make the button invisible.

3. `setOpaque(boolean opaque)`: 
   - This method serves to control whether the button is opaque or not. 
   - If `true`, the button is opaque, meaning it will block the background color, effectively making it appear invisible. If `false`, the button is translucent, allowing the background color to show through.

4. `setForeground(Color foreground)`: 
   - This method serves to set the foreground color of the button. 
   - By setting the foreground color to the same color as the background, you can effectively make the button invisible.

