To redirect System Streams to a JTextArea, you would use the following code:

```java
import javax.swing.*;
import java.awt.*;
import java.io.PrintStream;
import java.lang.reflect.Field;

public class RedirectStreamsToTextArea {
    public static void main(String[] args) throws NoSuchFieldException, IllegalAccessException {
        // Create a JTextArea
        JTextArea textArea = new JTextArea(20, 40);

        // Get the System.out and System.err streams
        PrintStream originalOut = System.out;
        PrintStream originalErr = System.err;

        // Redirect the streams to the JTextArea
        Field outField = PrintStream.class.getDeclaredField("out");
        outField.setAccessible(true);
        outField.set(System.out, textArea);

        Field errField = PrintStream.class.getDeclaredField("err");
        errField.setAccessible(true);
        errField.set(System.err, textArea);

        // Execute the code that redirects the streams on the AWT event dispatching thread
        SwingUtilities.invokeLater(() -> {
            // Code that writes to the streams
            System.out.println("Hello World!");
            System.err.println("Error message!");
        });

        // Restore the original streams
        outField.set(System.out, originalOut);
        errField.set(System.err, originalErr);
    }
}
```

This code creates a JTextArea, redirects the System Streams to it, executes some code that writes to the streams, and then restores the original streams.

