This method serves the purpose of updating the checksum with a single byte. It is useful when you need to process a byte at a time, rather than all at once.

### `update(byte[] b)`

This method serves the purpose of updating the checksum with an array of bytes. It is useful when you need to process a large amount of data, rather than a single byte.

### `getValue()`

This method serves the purpose of retrieving the current checksum value. It is useful when you need to access the final checksum value after processing all the data.

