1. `java.lang.Math.cos()`: This method serves to calculate the cosine of an angle, which is used to determine the x-coordinate of a point on a circle or an arc. In the context of drawing a rounded rectangle, it's used to calculate the x-coordinates of the rounded corners.

2. `java.lang.Math.sin()`: This method calculates the sine of an angle, which is used to determine the y-coordinate of a point on a circle or an arc. In the context of drawing a rounded rectangle, it's used to calculate the y-coordinates of the rounded corners.

Here's a simple example of how you can use these methods to draw a rounded rectangle in OpenGL:

```java
public class RoundedRectangle {
    public static void drawRoundedRectangle(float x, float y, float width, float height, float cornerRadius) {
        // Draw top-left corner
        glBegin(GL_QUADS);
        glVertex2f(x, y);
        glVertex2f(x + width, y);
        glVertex2f(x + width, y + height);
        glVertex2f(x, y + height);
        glEnd();

        // Draw top-right corner
        glBegin(GL_QUADS);
        glVertex2f(x + width - cornerRadius, y);
        glVertex2f(x + width, y);
        glVertex2f(x + width, y + height);
        glVertex2f(x + width - cornerRadius, y + height);
        glEnd();

        // Draw bottom-right corner
        glBegin(GL_QUADS);
        glVertex2f(x + width - cornerRadius, y + height);
        glVertex2f(x + width, y + height);
        glVertex2f(x + width, y + height - cornerRadius);
        glVertex2f(x + width - cornerRadius, y + height - cornerRadius);
        glEnd();

        // Draw bottom-left corner
        glBegin(GL_QUADS);
        glVertex2f(x, y + height - cornerRadius);
        glVertex2f(x, y + height);
        glVertex2f(x + width - cornerRadius, y + height);
        glVertex2f(x, y + height - cornerRadius);
        glEnd();

        // Draw top arc
        glBegin(GL_QUADS);
        glVertex2f(x, y);
        glVertex2f(x + width, y);
        glVertex2f(x + width * (1 - cornerRadius / width), y + height);
        glVertex2f(x, y + height * (1 - cornerRadius / height));
        glEnd();

        // Draw right arc
        glBegin(GL_QUADS);
        glVertex2f(x + width, y);
        glVertex2f(x + width, y + height);
        glVertex2f(x + width, y + height * (1 - cornerRadius / height));
        glVertex2f(x + width - cornerRadius, y + height);
        glEnd();

        // Draw left arc
        glBegin(GL_QUADS);
        glVertex2f(x, y + height - cornerRadius);
        glVertex2f(x, y + height);
        glVertex2f(x, y + height * (1 - cornerRadius / height));
        glVertex2f(x - cornerRadius, y + height);
        glEnd();

        // Draw bottom arc
        glBegin(GL_QUADS);
        glVertex2f(x - cornerRadius, y + height);
        glVertex2f(x, y + height);
        glVertex2f(x, y + height * (1 - cornerRadius / width));
        glVertex2f(x - cornerRadius, y);
        glEnd();
    }
}
```

This code draws a rounded rectangle by first drawing the corners and then drawing the arcs that connect the corners

