Here's how you can get the Soap Action URI from the operation's soap:operation extensibility element in Java:

```java
import javax.xml.namespace.QName;
import javax.xml.namespace.NamespaceContext;
import javax.xml.namespace.QName;

public class SoapActionURI {
    public static String getSoapActionURI(String soapOperation) {
        // Parse the soap:operation element
        String[] parts = soapOperation.split("soap:operation=");
        if (parts.length < 2) {
            return null;
        }
        String operation = parts[1].trim();

        // Extract the local part of the QName
        String localPart = operation.split(" ")[0];

        // Get the namespace URI
        String namespaceURI = "http://schemas.xmlsoap.org/wsdl/operation";

        // Create a QName
        QName qname = new QName(namespaceURI, localPart);

        // Get the local part of the QName
        String soapAction = qname.getLocalPart();

        return soapAction;
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String soapOperation = "<soap:operation soapAction=\"http://example.com/MyOperation\"/>";
        String soapActionURI = getSoapActionURI(soapOperation);
        System.out.println(soapActionURI);  // Output: MyOperation
    }
}
```

Here's an explanation of each API method:

- `javax.xml.namespace.QName.getLocalPart()`: This method serves to retrieve the local part of a QName, which is the part of the QName that comes before the namespace URI. This is useful for extracting the operation name from the soap:operation element.

