3. `java.util.concurrent.Executors.newSingleThreadExecutor()`: This method creates a new single-threaded executor service. It serves the purpose of creating a single thread that can be used to execute tasks.

4. `Thread.currentThread()`: This method returns the current thread. It serves the purpose of getting the current thread that is executing the code.

