- `java.util.concurrent.ThreadPoolExecutor.awaitTermination()`: This method blocks until all tasks have completed execution after a shutdown request, or the timeout occurs, or the current thread is interrupted. It serves as a way to wait for the completion of all tasks in the executor, ensuring that the program doesn't proceed until all tasks have finished.

