Here's a Java function that returns a vector containing all the notes from all Notes that are playing at tick in MIDI:

```java
import javax.sound.midi.MidiSystem;
import javax.sound.midi.MidiUnavailableException;
import javax.sound.midi.Synthesizer;
import javax.sound.midi.Track;
import javax.sound.midi.MidiChannel;
import java.util.ArrayList;
import java.util.List;

public class MidiNotes {
    public static List<String> getPlayingNotes(int tick) {
        Synthesizer synthesizer = MidiSystem.getSynthesizer();
        synthesizer.open();
        Track track = synthesizer.getTracks()[0];
        List<String> playingNotes = new ArrayList<>();

        for (int i = 0; i < track.getEvents().size(); i++) {
            MidiEvent event = track.getEvents().get(i);
            MidiChannel channel = ((MidiEvent) event).getChannel();

            if (event.getTick() == tick) {
                if (channel.getProgramChange() == 0) {
                    playingNotes.add(getNoteName(channel.getNoteOn()));
                } else if (channel.getNoteOff() != 0) {
                    playingNotes.remove(getNoteName(channel.getNoteOff()));
                }
            }
        }

        synthesizer.close();
        return playingNotes;
    }

    private static String getNoteName(int note) {
        String[] notes = {"C", "C#", "D", "D#", "E", "F", "F#", "G", "G#", "A", "A#", "B"};
        int octave = note / 12 - 1;
        int noteNumber = note % 12;
        return notes[noteNumber] + octave;
    }
}
```

Here's a breakdown of the Java API methods used:

- `MidiSystem.getSynthesizer()`: This method serves to retrieve a synthesizer object, which is used to interact with the MIDI system. It is the entry point for creating a MIDI synthesizer.

- `synthesizer.open()`: This method serves to open the synthesizer, which is necessary before using it. It initializes the synthesizer and prepares it for use.

- `track.getEvents()`: This method serves to retrieve a list of events that are currently being played on the track. The events are stored in time order, meaning that the most recent event is at the end of the list.

- `event.getTick()`: This method serves to retrieve the tick number of the event. The tick number represents the time at which the event occurred.

- `channel.getProgramChange()`: This method serves to retrieve the program change event of the channel. A program change event is used to change the program (or sound) of the channel.

- `channel.getNoteOn()`: This method serves to retrieve the note on event of the channel. A note on event is used to turn on a note.

- `channel.getNoteOff()`: This method serves to retrieve the note off event of the channel. A note off event is used to turn off a note.

- `channel.getChannel()`: This method serves to retrieve the MIDI channel number of the event.

- `synthesizer.close()`: This method serves to close the synthesizer, which is necessary after using it to free up system resources.

