Here's how you can embed an XML file into a Java package and access it using the provided Java API methods:

### Embedding XML File

First, you need to add the XML file to your Java package. You can do this by placing the XML file in the root directory of your project, alongside your Java classes.

### Accessing XML File using Class.getResourceAsStream()

To access the XML file, you can use the `Class.getResourceAsStream()` method. This method serves the following purpose:

* Finds a resource with a given name, which in this case is the path to the XML file.

Here's an example of how to use this method:

```java
import java.io.InputStream;
import java.io.InputStreamReader;
import java.io.BufferedReader;

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        // Get the class loader
        ClassLoader classLoader = Main.class.getClassLoader();

        // Get the absolute resource name
        String resourceName = "/path/to/your/xml/file.xml";

        // Get the input stream
        InputStream inputStream = classLoader.getResourceAsStream(resourceName);

        // Check if the resource is found
        if (inputStream != null) {
            // Read the XML file
            BufferedReader reader = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(inputStream));
            String line;
            while ((line = reader.readLine()) != null) {
                System.out.println(line);
            }
            reader.close();
        } else {
            System.out.println("Resource not found");
        }
    }
}
```

