- `String.charAt(index)`: This method returns the char value at the specified index. It serves the purpose of getting the ASCII value of each character in the sequence.

- `int - 33`: This is a simple arithmetic operation that subtracts 33 from the ASCII value of each character. It serves the purpose of calculating the phred score for each character.

- `byte cast`: This is a cast operation that converts an integer value to a byte value. It serves the purpose of storing the phred score in the byte array.

