5. `java.util.regex.Matcher.appendTail()`: This method appends the remaining characters of the input sequence to the result string. It serves the purpose of appending the remaining characters of the input sequence to the result string after all matches have been found.

Note: The `[^\\x00-\\x7F]` pattern matches any character that is not in the ASCII range (0-127). The `\\x00-\\x7F` is a range of ASCII characters. The `^` symbol inside the square brackets negates the match, so `[^\\x00-\\x7F]` matches any character that is not in the ASCII range.

