public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String str = "HelloWorld";
        Pattern pattern = Pattern.compile("(?<=\\D)(?=[A-Z])");
        Matcher matcher = pattern.matcher(str);
        StringBuffer buffer = new StringBuffer();
        while (matcher.find()) {
            matcher.appendReplacement(buffer, " ");
        }
        matcher.appendTail(buffer);
        System.out.println(buffer.toString());  // Output: "H e l l o W o r l d"
    }
}
```

This method serves to suppress the special meaning of certain characters in the replacement string, allowing them to be treated as literal characters. In this case, the `Matcher.quoteReplacement()` method is used to prevent the backslash (`\\`) from being interpreted as an escape character.

