Here's an explanation of the Java API methods for reading a file from a ZIP archive:

1. `java.util.zip.ZipFile`: This class represents a ZIP file and provides methods for reading its contents. It serves as the entry point for working with ZIP files.

2. `java.util.zip.ZipEntry`: This class represents a single entry (file or directory) within a ZIP archive. It provides information about the entry, such as its name and size.

3. `java.util.zip.ZipInputStream`: This class represents an input stream for reading the contents of a ZIP archive. It serves as a bridge between the ZIP file and the application code, allowing for reading the contents of the archive.

4. `java.util.zip.ZipFile.getInputStream()`: This method returns an input stream for reading the contents of the specified zip file entry. It serves as a way to read the contents of a specific entry within the ZIP archive.

5. `java.util.zip.ZipEntry.getName()`: This method returns the name of the ZIP entry. It serves as a way to identify the entry within the archive.

6. `java.util.zip.ZipEntry.getSize()`: This method returns the size of the ZIP entry. It serves as a way to determine the size of the entry within the archive.

Here's an example of how to read a file from a ZIP archive using these API methods:

```java
import java.io.FileInputStream;
import java.io.IOException;
import java.util.zip.ZipEntry;
import java.util.zip.ZipFile;
import java.util.zip.ZipInputStream;

public class ZipFileReader {

    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {
        // Open the ZIP file
        ZipFile zipFile = new ZipFile("example.zip");

        // Get the input stream for the desired entry
        ZipEntry entry = zipFile.getEntry("path/to/file.txt");
        if (entry != null) {
            // Create a new input stream for the entry
            ZipInputStream zipInputStream = new ZipInputStream(zipFile.getInputStream(entry));

            // Read the contents of the entry
            byte[] buffer = new byte[1024];
            int bytesRead;
            while ((bytesRead = zipInputStream.read(buffer)) != -1) {
                System.out.println(new String(buffer, 0, bytesRead));
            }
        } else {
            System.out.println("Entry not found");
        }

        // Close the input streams
        zipInputStream.close();
        zipFile.close();
    }
}
```

This code opens a ZIP file, gets the input stream for a specific entry, reads the contents of the entry, and closes the input streams when finished.

