Here's how you can convert a number into Roman Numerals using Java. I'll also explain each API method used.

### Roman Numeral Conversion

```java
public class RomanNumeralConverter {

    private static final String[] ROMAN_NUMERALS = {"M", "CM", "D", "CD", "C", "XC", "L", "XL", "X", "IX", "V", "IV", "I"};
    private static final int[] VALUES = {1000, 900, 500, 400, 100, 90, 50, 40, 10, 9, 5, 4, 1};

    public static String convertToRomanNumeral(int number) {
        StringBuilder romanNumeral = new StringBuilder();

        for (int i = 0; i < VALUES.length; i++) {
            while (number >= VALUES[i]) {
                romanNumeral.append(ROMAN_NUMERALS[i]);
                number -= VALUES[i];
            }
        }

        return romanNumeral.toString();
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println(convertToRomanNumeral(4));  // IV
        System.out.println(convertToRomanNumeral(9));  // IX
        System.out.println(convertToRomanNumeral(13)); // XIII
        System.out.println(convertToRomanNumeral(44)); // XLIV
        System.out.println(convertToRomanNumeral(1000)); // M
    }
}
```

