Here's the Java code to calculate the standard deviation of all elements in an array:

```java
import java.lang.Math;

public class Main {

    public static double calculateStandardDeviation(double[] array) {
        double sum = 0;
        for (double num : array) {
            sum += num;
        }
        double mean = sum / array.length;

        double sumSquares = 0;
        for (double num : array) {
            sumSquares += Math.pow(num - mean, 2);
        }
        double variance = sumSquares / array.length;

        return Math.sqrt(variance);
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        double[] array = {1, 2, 3, 4, 5};
        double standardDeviation = calculateStandardDeviation(array);
        System.out.println("Standard Deviation: " + standardDeviation);
    }
}
```

Here's an explanation of the Java API methods used:

