Here's a simple Java function that normalizes the input array to double values between -1.0 and 1.0:

```java
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        double[] array = {10, 20, 30, 40, 50};
        double[] normalizedArray = normalizeArray(array);
        for (double value : normalizedArray) {
            System.out.println(value);
        }
    }

    public static double[] normalizeArray(double[] array) {
        double min = Double.MAX_VALUE;
        double max = Double.MIN_VALUE;
        for (double value : array) {
            if (value < min) {
                min = value;
            }
            if (value > max) {
                max = value;
            }
        }

        double[] normalizedArray = new double[array.length];
        for (int i = 0; i < array.length; i++) {
            normalizedArray[i] = (array[i] - min) / (max - min);
        }

        return normalizedArray;
    }
}
```

This function first finds the minimum and maximum values in the input array. Then it calculates the normalized values by subtracting the minimum value and dividing by the range of the input values. The result is an array of double values between -1.0 and 1.0.

