Here's how you can get the file name from the server request using the provided Java API methods:

```java
import java.net.HttpURLConnection;
import java.net.URL;
import java.util.Enumeration;

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {
        URL url = new URL("http://example.com/path/to/file.txt");
        HttpURLConnection connection = (HttpURLConnection) url.openConnection();
        connection.setRequestMethod("GET");

        // Get the file name from the 'Content-Disposition' header
        String fileName = getFileNameFromHeader(connection, "Content-Disposition");

        // Get the file name from the 'Content-Disposition' header with a parameter
        String fileNameWithParam = getFileNameFromHeader(connection, "Content-Disposition", "filename");

        // Get the file name from the 'Content-Disposition' header with a parameter and a suffix
        String fileNameWithSuffix = getFileNameFromHeader(connection, "Content-Disposition", "filename*=UTF-8''example.txt");

        System.out.println("File name from 'Content-Disposition' header: " + fileName);
        System.out.println("File name from 'Content-Disposition' header with a parameter: " + fileNameWithParam);
        System.out.println("File name from 'Content-Disposition' header with a parameter and a suffix: " + fileNameWithSuffix);
    }

    private static String getFileNameFromHeader(HttpURLConnection connection, String headerName) throws Exception {
        Enumeration<String> headerNames = connection.getHeaderFieldNames();
        while (headerNames.hasMoreElements()) {
            String headerName = headerNames.nextElement();
            if (headerName.equals(headerName)) {
                return connection.getHeaderField(headerName);
            }
        }
        return null;
    }

    private static String getFileNameFromHeader(HttpURLConnection connection, String headerName, String param) throws Exception {
        Enumeration<String> headerNames = connection.getHeaderFieldNames();
        while (headerNames.hasMoreElements()) {
            String headerName = headerNames.nextElement();
            if (headerName.equals(headerName)) {
                String headerValue = connection.getHeaderField(headerName);
                if (headerValue != null && headerValue.contains(param)) {
                    int index = headerValue.indexOf(param);
                    int endIndex = headerValue.indexOf("=", index);
                    if (endIndex != -1) {
                        return headerValue.substring(index + param.length(), endIndex);
                    }
                }
            }
        }
        return null;
    }
}
```

Here's what each API method does and which part of the request it serves:

1. `java.net.HttpURLConnection.getHeaderField()`: This method returns the value for the nth header field. It serves to retrieve the value of a specific header field from the HTTP request.

2. `java.net.HttpURLConnection.getHeaderFieldKey()`: This method returns the key of the nth header field. It serves to iterate through all the headers in the message and retrieve their keys.

3. `java.net.HttpURLConnection.getHeaderFieldNames()`: This method returns an enumeration of the header field names. It serves to iterate through all the header field names in the message.

The 'Content-Disposition' header is used to specify the disposition of the response body, including the file name. The file name can be specified as a parameter in the header, and it can also be specified with a suffix. The `getFileNameFromHeader` method is used to extract the file name from the 'Content-Disposition' header.

